# The whole fleet crontab: ONE line per box (two on the triage box). All
# locking, logging and evidence lines live inside tick.sh — the cron line
# carries no flock and no redirect, so it can never drift per box again
# (five hand-edited variants did).
#
# Every box:
*/5 * * * * $HOME/duty/bin/tick.sh
#
# Triage box only — the operator notifier is a fleet singleton:
#*/5 * * * * $HOME/duty/bin/tick.sh notify
#
# Hygiene has NO cron line: it self-schedules hourly inside the duty tick,
# under the same lock, so it can never race the triage sweep over shared
# checkouts (the old separate hygiene cron could, and did).
